      "statusChangeNewStatus": "needs more information",
      "value": "I'm unable to reproduce this issue. I have no issues getting 120 fps on a 120hz monitor or 90 fps on a 90hz vr headset. This could be normal if you are using a 60hz monitor in desktop mode, as it was changed to match your monitor several updates ago. If not, then we'll need more information such as what hardware you're using, what platform you're using to access VRChat, and what software you may have running in the background that could be locking your framerate such as Rivatuner.\nAdditionally, if you have multiple monitors that are set to different refresh rates, you can change which one VRChat launches onto by using the -monitor [n] launch parameter. VRchat will use the refresh rate of that monitor.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
